; Minimal main scene so the fixture project can actually RUN.
;
; The fixture was built to validate the editor-presence SELECTION path, which
; needs no scene at all — so it shipped without one, and without
; `run/main_scene`. That is fine until Play/Stop (task #48), at which point
; `play_main_scene()` has nothing to launch and Godot prompts the user instead
; of running, which is indistinguishable from our command silently failing.
;
; The attached script prints a line on _ready and on exit. That is the point:
; a Godot window appearing proves a window appeared. The stdout line proves the
; GAME actually started, which is the claim Play/Stop has to make.

[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://main.gd" id="1"]

[node name="Main" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("1")
